   "source": [
    "# PDAS CA2\n",
    "# Do graduates prioritise salary or company stability when choosing jobs in Singapore?\n",
    "This study investigates whether graduates in Singapore prioritise higher salaries or employment stability when choosing jobs. As employment preferences are not directly captured in labour market datasets, indicators such as gross monthly income are used to represent salary outcomes, while employment stability is proxied through measures including full-time permanent employment and job tenure. By analysing salary and stability trends across educational attainment levels and over time, this study aims to identify potential trade-offs between income levels and job security among graduates in Singapore.\n"
   ]
  },
